    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Cape Town spreads around Table Bay below Table Mountain, whose flat summit stands about 1,085 metres high. The Cape Peninsula runs south from the city to Cape Point, with cold Atlantic beaches on its west side and False Bay on its east.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The Dutch East India Company set up a supply station here in 1652. The Cape Malay families of the Bo-Kaap keep their painted houses, their bobotie and their koeksisters. Nelson Mandela spent 18 years in prison on Robben Island, out in the bay.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "December to March is dry and hot, though the south-easter can blow for days. Check that the cableway is running before you head up, as wind closes it.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
